                <pb facs="0762" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.48/3080</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-20T23:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 20, 1916, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>286. Department has repeatedly made it known to you and to American Relief
                    Committee that no funds are available for indefinite <pb facs="0763" n="687"
                        xml:id="pg687"/> maintenance destitute Americans in Mexico. Red Cross has
                    made similar announcement. Therefore, in view present economic conditions and of
                    political situation in Mexico, all Americans whose presence in Mexico City is
                    not absolutely essential for business reasons should be advised to return
                    immediately to this country. You will furnish transportation in accordance with
                    previous instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
